1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:06,950
This is a multidisciplinary tumour board. Different
specialists, bringing their expertise to one patient's care.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:14,300
Before they can agree a plan, they must bring the scans,
pathology, treatment history and evidence together.

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:21,750
MDT Observatory explores a different way to prepare. Each
specialist has a role-specific agent.

4
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:29,250
The oncology agent reviews treatment. Radiology examines
imaging. Pathology brings the tissue findings.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,500
The agent represents a professional perspective. The
specialist steers the work and remains responsible for
clinical judgement.

6
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:47,700
A model interprets information and communicates. Tools
retrieve the records and evidence the role is allowed to use.

7
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:54,500
Its role and case context focus the work. These are curated
sources, with access limits visible.

8
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:59,700
This film shows the application's scripted rehearsal, not live
model inference.

9
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:03,850
Everyone sees the same case. Their working views are
different.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,300
Imaging and tissue findings. Treatment and surgery.

11
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,450
The chair sees the shared questions and where the specialties
disagree.

12
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:21,600
The agents publish positions into a shared meeting. The chair
coordinates the unresolved questions.

13
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:29,250
In this synthetic case, treatment has reduced the liver
disease. But response alone does not settle the next step.

14
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:36,500
Can every original liver site be addressed? What does the
small, indeterminate lung nodule mean?

15
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:43,600
And how well does the evidence support this particular
sequence of treatment? Those questions need attention.

16
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:51,800
When evidence is incomplete, the uncertainty stays visible.
The system asks for specialist input.

17
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:58,700
Here, the radiologist asks for review of all nine liver sites,
vessel margins and the lung nodule.

18
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:04,100
That guidance returns to the discussion. Remaining conditions
stay attached.

19
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:11,800
A conditional plan now comes back for review. Required human
concurrence is tied to this exact version.

20
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:19,700
The aim is less time assembling facts, and more time on
judgement. Agreement does not remove uncertainty.

21
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:25,300
The recorded outcome carries the actions, conditions and
review history forward.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,850
With a model connected, it can draft a colleague letter and a
patient summary for named clinician approval.

23
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:39,410
Drafting is unavailable in this local run. These illustrated
excerpts show the intended communication.

24
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:44,700
Plain language. The patient's language. Always reviewed before
sharing.

25
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,350
Let the agents prepare, search, compare and coordinate.

26
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:57,150
Give specialists more time for the difficult questions, the
patient's priorities, and the judgement that remains theirs.
